      "id": "ev_1",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_Chinese-targeting-IndianPowerGrid-ta-2022-0406(04-06-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "executive_summary",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s1"
      },
      "text": "In February 2021, Recorded Future’s Insikt Group reported on intrusion activity targeting operational assets within India’s power grid that we attributed to a likely Chinese state-sponsored threat activity group we track as RedEcho.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_2",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_Chinese-targeting-IndianPowerGrid-ta-2022-0406(04-06-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "executive_summary",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s2"
      },
      "text": "Following a short lull after the publication of our RedEcho reporting, we have detected ongoing targeting of Indian power grid organizations by China- linked adversaries, frequently using the privately shared modular backdoor ShadowPad.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_4",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_Chinese-targeting-IndianPowerGrid-ta-2022-0406(04-06-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "executive_summary",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s4"
      },
      "text": "In recent months, we observed likely network intrusions targeting at least 7 Indian State Load Despatch Centres (SLDCs) responsible for carrying out real-time operations for grid control and electricity dispatch within these respective states.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_5",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_Chinese-targeting-IndianPowerGrid-ta-2022-0406(04-06-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "executive_summary",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s5"
      },
      "text": "In addition to the targeting of power grid assets, we also identified the compromise of a national emergency response system and the Indian subsidiary of a multinational logistics company by the same threat activity group.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_6",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_Chinese-targeting-IndianPowerGrid-ta-2022-0406(04-06-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "executive_summary",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s6"
      },
      "text": "To achieve this, the group likely compromised and co- opted internet-facing DVR/IP camera devices for command and control (C2) of Shadowpad malware infections, as well as use of the open source tool FastReverseProxy (FRP) .",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_7",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_Chinese-targeting-IndianPowerGrid-ta-2022-0406(04-06-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "executive_summary",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s7"
      },
      "text": "At this time, we have not identified technical evidence allowing us to attribute it to RedEcho, and we are currently clustering this latest activity under the temporary group name Threat Activity Group 38 (TAG- 38) 1 .",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
